 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "ZhBu7Ur8AAAJ",
   "from": "Echo",
   "author": "9de1ea290205e9e4",
   "date": "2020-04-09T02:53:55Z",
   "subject": "How to no display the tippoint outside my external data.frame",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear prof. Yu,<div><br></div><div>I used the %&gt;+% to map my external data to the tree. The data was one part of the tree. I just want to show my data in the tree but not others.   (grey color points is not my data)</div><div><br></div><div>The code:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">tre&lt;-read.tree(&quot;HA&quot;)</span><br></div><div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">location&lt;-read.csv(paste0(&quot;Location.csv&quot;))</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">p_L&lt;-ggtree(tre) %&lt;+% location</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">p3&lt;-p_L+geom_tippoint(aes(color = Location))</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">p3</span></div></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Result</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><a style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/fc4aed6e1066/Rplot01xxx.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Rplot01xxx.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"273\" border=\"0\"></a><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thanks for your help.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Best wishes.</span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "aaBmPSKKBAAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "2a4584b898b0bd00",
   "date": "2020-04-09T03:36:10Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to no display the tippoint outside my external data.frame",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">First of all,  don’t copy paste your code trunk. Without your data, we usually can’t help.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">It would be better to provide minimal reproducible example.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">An example like this is more suitable:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">x = rtree(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">10</span>)\r\nd = data.frame(label = c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;t1&#39;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39;t2&#39;</span>), location=c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;GZ&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;HK&quot;</span>))\r\nggtree(x) %&lt;+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=location))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This is an issue of ggplot2, which always translate NA value as a separate category by default. Such behavior can be disable in <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_color_xxx</code>, e.g. :</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\"> ggtree(x) %&lt;+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=location)) + \r\n    scale_color_manual(values=c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;red&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;blue&quot;</span>), na.translate=<span>F</span>)\r\n</code></pre></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Thu, Apr 9, 2020 at 10:53 AM Echo <a href=\"http://mailto:lxp...@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:lxp...@gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482127816000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19J_2olInTMnC0tQFxf1ZI\">lxpen...@gmail.com</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
